Ben, You're likely not going to remember this issue where I have a matrix of ordered scores, y[i,d], where the number of categories depends on "d".   the ordered_logistic() distribution cannot address such a case.  You suggested a patch to the templated function ordered_logistic.hpp of the form:

int K = c.size() + 1;

becomes

int K = max(y);

This won't work because ordered_logistic is univariate (so that 'y' is an integer).   Setting int K = y won't work because y may not hold the maximum possible value for y[,d].   The immediate approach I think of, at present, is to edit my copy of ordered_logistic.hpp to take in a (new) integer indicator for "K" (set to max(y[,d]).  Before I made the change on my end, I would appreciate to have your input about whether you think such is okay.

terrance.

