Thanks for these useful discussions.

Hurdle count models are two-component models with a truncated (at zero) count
component (y = 1, 2, 3, ....) for positive counts and a hurdle component that models the
zero counts. See http://rss.acs.unt.edu/Rdoc/library/pscl/html/hurdle.html.

I found other typos in the recent stan-ref 1.0.3-2 :
(1) Page 132: in the Bernoulli pmf, c and y are mixed
(2) Poisson distribution (bottom line of Page 134): lambda! should be ”n!“.
(3) Page 133: for Categorical Distribution, y and n are mixed.

###############################################

